[Do-Hyeon]<i> Why hello. Chairman Ju.</i>
<i>To what do I owe this pleasure?</i>

256
00:20:21.261 --> 00:20:22.262
I'm sorry. sir.

257
00:20:24.014 --> 00:20:27.851
You're in here by yourself.
but you set up this chair like this.

258
00:20:29.269 --> 00:20:30.646
Maybe you had a guest over.

259
00:20:33.357 --> 00:20:35.400
Juhak Construction's chairman.

260
00:20:36.109 --> 00:20:37.402
Ju Gang-chan's your name. right?

261
00:20:40.739 --> 00:20:42.032
Yeah. that's my name.

262
00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:44.785
And who are you?

263
00:20:45.994 --> 00:20:48.747
Well. let's just say
I'm a civil servant. hmm?

264
00:20:53.919 --> 00:20:55.587
I doubt you're with the police.

265
00:20:57.089 --> 00:20:58.090
The NIS?

266
00:20:58.840 --> 00:21:01.176
Or maybe the SMD?

267
00:21:03.595 --> 00:21:05.055
[chuckles]

268
00:21:05.555 --> 00:21:07.432
You seem to know a lot for a civilian.

269
00:21:07.516 --> 00:21:10.102
It sounds like you play golf
with people in government.

270
00:21:10.185 --> 00:21:12.646
-Hmm? [chuckles]
-[Ju chuckles]

271
00:21:12.729 --> 00:21:14.523
Let's stop wasting our time then.

272
00:21:16.108 --> 00:21:18.819
I'm the director
of the SMD of South Korea.

273
00:21:20.195 --> 00:21:22.489
And I'm looking for a girl
named Kim Min-ji.

274
00:21:22.572 --> 00:21:24.074
I tracked her to this location.

275
00:21:25.284 --> 00:21:28.287
I know she's here.
so hurry up and bring her out now.

276
00:21:31.498 --> 00:21:32.499
Listen.

277
00:21:33.083 --> 00:21:35.168
You can barge in here.
break down the gates.

278
00:21:35.252 --> 00:21:36.503
I don't care.

279
00:21:37.963 --> 00:21:39.715
But I can't stand smoking.

280
00:21:49.141 --> 00:21:51.560
Hey. shithead. I guess you can't tell
your head from your ass

281
00:21:51.643 --> 00:21:53.270
'cause I've been treating you civilly.

282
00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:57.357
Bring me Kim Min-ji
while I'm still asking nicely.

283
00:21:58.692 --> 00:22:01.153
Just how much power does
your agency actually have?

284
00:22:02.279 --> 00:22:05.365
Enough that you can bust in here
and threaten a civilian like this?

285
00:22:10.746 --> 00:22:11.747
Hey. Ju Gang-chan.

286
00:22:13.332 --> 00:22:15.625
Don't you see
the deep shit you're in. huh?

287
00:22:17.294 --> 00:22:19.629
My agents have your house surrounded.

288
00:22:20.464 --> 00:22:22.966
This operation's sanctioned.
you little shit.

289
00:22:25.177 --> 00:22:27.429
-No luck?
-She's not in any of the rooms upstairs.

290
00:22:27.512 --> 00:22:28.680
Not in the basement either.

291
00:22:28.764 --> 00:22:30.807
-[agents grunting]
-What's that?

292
00:22:34.102 --> 00:22:35.103
[grunts]

293
00:22:35.854 --> 00:22:37.981
[grunts. groans]

294
00:22:42.903 --> 00:22:43.945
Don't move.

295
00:22:44.946 --> 00:22:47.866
You guy's are trespassing.
This is private property.

296
00:22:47.949 --> 00:22:49.785
This operation's sanctioned!

297
00:22:58.418 --> 00:23:00.003
Stop or I'll shoot!

298
00:23:02.589 --> 00:23:04.299
You don't have the balls.

299
00:23:17.437 --> 00:23:18.522
[Han-soo] Damn it.

300
00:23:18.605 --> 00:23:20.899
Looks like the SMD folks beat us here.

301
00:23:20.982 --> 00:23:22.067
What should we do?

302
00:23:22.776 --> 00:23:24.861
Well. I guess it doesn't matter
who goes first.

303
00:23:25.946 --> 00:23:27.614
-Ready to go inside?
-We can't.

304
00:23:27.697 --> 00:23:31.409
The SMD and Ju Gang-chan.
they both want her for their own reasons.

305
00:23:31.493 --> 00:23:34.412
If we rush in without a plan.
it would put her in more danger.

306
00:23:36.331 --> 00:23:38.583
So we're just gonna stand by
and do nothing?

307
00:23:45.799 --> 00:23:49.010
Wait. Aren't those the people
who helped us earlier?

308
00:24:05.652 --> 00:24:07.362
Let's split up.

309
00:24:08.488 --> 00:24:09.614
You go ahead.

310
00:24:10.615 --> 00:24:12.576
[grunts. groans]

311
00:24:13.577 --> 00:24:14.828
[coughs]

312
00:24:17.414 --> 00:24:20.417
Seems to me that you're the one
who's in deep shit now.

313
00:24:22.043 --> 00:24:23.211
[phone buzzing]

314
00:24:28.675 --> 00:24:30.552
-Yes. hello Minister.
<i>-</i>[minister] <i>You idiot!</i>

315
00:24:31.094 --> 00:24:32.804
<i>What the hell are you doing there?</i>

316
00:24:33.346 --> 00:24:35.182
-Sir?
-[minister]<i> Leave now!</i>

317
00:24:35.265 --> 00:24:36.433
-But sirâ€¦
-[call ends]

318
00:24:47.944 --> 00:24:49.279
Get up. We're leaving.

319
00:24:49.362 --> 00:24:50.864
[agent groans] Okay. Sorry. sir.

320
00:25:02.959 --> 00:25:04.252
[stones crunching]

321
00:25:04.961 --> 00:25:06.421
[shushes]

322
00:25:42.040 --> 00:25:43.041
[sighs]

323
00:25:57.389 --> 00:25:59.683
How much did he cough up
to have a government official

324
00:25:59.766 --> 00:26:01.393
in his back pocket like this?

325
00:26:14.239 --> 00:26:15.240
[Guk-cheol] Damn it.

326
00:26:16.574 --> 00:26:17.867
Everyone. fall back!

327
00:26:49.566 --> 00:26:50.984
{\an8}SUNG HAN-SOO

328
00:28:13.274 --> 00:28:16.111
[dramatic music plays]

329
00:28:35.713 --> 00:28:37.048
All clear.

330
00:28:44.055 --> 00:28:45.849
[shushes. mouthing words]

331
00:28:51.646 --> 00:28:52.689
[grunting]

332
00:28:54.149 --> 00:28:55.859
-Who's that?
-What? [laughs]

333
00:28:55.942 --> 00:28:57.360
Hello. gentlemen!

334
00:28:57.444 --> 00:28:59.028
Dry cleaner at your service

335
00:28:59.112 --> 00:29:02.449
Looks like we got a wrinkle.
but we'll iron it out. [chuckles]

336
00:29:06.035 --> 00:29:07.036
[shouts]

337
00:29:13.042 --> 00:29:16.296
-[groaning]
-[electricity buzzing]

338
00:29:37.442 --> 00:29:38.485
Min-ji!

339
00:29:39.402 --> 00:29:41.070
Min-ji! Hey. Hold on.

340
00:29:41.154 --> 00:29:42.989
[grunting. muffled]

341
00:29:43.072 --> 00:29:44.157
You okay. Min-ji?

342
00:29:45.116 --> 00:29:46.951
Mister. what are you doing here?

343
00:29:47.827 --> 00:29:52.165
[panting] The dry cleaner's
is temporarily closed.

344
00:29:52.248 --> 00:29:53.917
Are you okay? Think you can walk?

345
00:29:54.959 --> 00:29:56.544
-Who are you?
-I'll explain later.

346
00:29:57.545 --> 00:29:58.630
-I don't understand what--
-It's okay.

347
00:29:58.713 --> 00:29:59.923
-We have to go.
-Come on.

348
00:30:04.260 --> 00:30:05.261
Hurry.

349
00:30:11.559 --> 00:30:12.811
Good work. you two.

350
00:30:13.728 --> 00:30:14.979
-Get her in.
-Yes. sir.

351
00:30:15.939 --> 00:30:17.857
Kim Min-ji. please come with us.

352
00:30:17.941 --> 00:30:19.984
-Who are you?
-It's okay.

353
00:30:20.860 --> 00:30:23.112
[Min-ji] Mister. Who are these people?

354
00:30:23.196 --> 00:30:24.197
Wait. sir!

355
00:30:24.823 --> 00:30:26.157
See you back at the office.

356
00:30:30.954 --> 00:30:32.914
-[door closes]
-[engine starts]

357
00:30:43.800 --> 00:30:45.134
Any updates?

358
00:30:48.012 --> 00:30:49.472
It's been quiet here. No movement.

359
00:30:49.556 --> 00:30:51.641
Have them watch the rear just in case.

360
00:30:51.724 --> 00:30:53.351
-We're heading back first.
-Yes. sir.

361
00:30:53.434 --> 00:30:57.188
All vehicles. watch the rear
until Vehicle 1 arrives at HQ.

362
00:30:57.272 --> 00:30:58.273
Okay. Copy that.

363
00:31:03.361 --> 00:31:04.529
Hey. sir?

364
00:31:05.280 --> 00:31:06.739
Thanks for saving me.

365
00:31:07.282 --> 00:31:08.408
But who are you guys?

366
00:31:16.124 --> 00:31:17.709
Where are we going right now?

367
00:31:19.043 --> 00:31:21.004
Let me contact my dad.

368
00:31:22.255 --> 00:31:23.590
Or I'll jump out of the car.

369
00:31:23.673 --> 00:31:24.966
[door handle rattling]

370
00:31:28.761 --> 00:31:29.929
Min-ji.

371
00:31:30.763 --> 00:31:33.349
You'll be fine.
but you have to trust us. okay?

372
00:31:33.433 --> 00:31:35.435
-Please. just let me call my--
-Okay.

373
00:31:36.728 --> 00:31:37.729
It's okay.

374
00:31:41.774 --> 00:31:45.153
[Guk-cheol] We can't tell you who we are.
That's just the nature of this job.

375
00:31:45.236 --> 00:31:46.529
We live in the shadows.

376
00:31:47.697 --> 00:31:49.741
A life where people don't know you exist.

377
00:31:50.700 --> 00:31:52.577
Out of sight. in the background.

378
00:31:59.083 --> 00:32:00.084
Nothing to report.

379
00:32:01.044 --> 00:32:02.045
[grunts]

380
00:32:04.839 --> 00:32:07.050
What the heck? Where'd he go?

381
00:32:14.807 --> 00:32:16.559
Shit. [breathes heavily]

382
00:32:26.110 --> 00:32:27.779
-[gun fires]
-[groans]

383
00:32:31.532 --> 00:32:33.201
[groaning]

384
00:32:34.869 --> 00:32:36.496
Where the hell did they take my daughter?

385
00:32:38.998 --> 00:32:42.335
They're going back to HQ. [groans]

386
00:32:54.055 --> 00:32:55.390
[radio beeps]

387
00:32:55.473 --> 00:32:57.976
[Kim. distorted] <i>Min-ji. Min-ji.</i>
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

388
00:32:58.059 --> 00:32:59.310
What's he saying?

389
00:32:59.394 --> 00:33:00.937
-Try another channel.
-[Jang] Yes. sir.

390
00:33:04.065 --> 00:33:06.693
Min-ji. Can you hear my voice?

391
00:33:06.776 --> 00:33:07.902
<i>Don't worry. everything will be fine.</i>

392
00:33:07.986 --> 00:33:09.862
<i>I'm coming to get you.</i>

393
00:33:09.946 --> 00:33:11.447
Min-ji. are you okay?

394
00:33:12.573 --> 00:33:13.992
<i>Can you hear me?</i>

395
00:33:14.075 --> 00:33:15.159
Min-ji!

396
00:33:15.243 --> 00:33:17.120
I can hear you. Agent Kim.

397
00:33:19.956 --> 00:33:22.250
If you so much as lay a finger
on my daughter.

398
00:33:23.793 --> 00:33:24.877
I'll kill all of you.

399
00:33:24.961 --> 00:33:27.255
[Guk-cheol] Wow. what a time to be alive.

400
00:33:27.338 --> 00:33:29.215
This is what freedom looks like in Korea.

401
00:33:29.298 --> 00:33:32.218
A goddamn spy having the nerve
to threaten the SMD Director.

402
00:33:32.301 --> 00:33:33.678
As soon as I get her backâ€¦

403
00:33:34.679 --> 00:33:35.888
I swear I'll surrender.

404
00:33:36.597 --> 00:33:38.349
[Guk-cheol]
Yeah. I remember what you said.

405
00:33:38.433 --> 00:33:40.101
I just don't know
if I can trust a spy's word.

406
00:33:41.394 --> 00:33:43.271
Turn yourself in first
as a sign of good faith.

407
00:33:43.354 --> 00:33:45.064
Can't do that until she's with me.

408
00:33:45.148 --> 00:33:46.816
Fine. I can play hardball. too.

409
00:33:47.400 --> 00:33:49.652
I'll keep your daughter company
while we wait. huh?

410
00:33:51.237 --> 00:33:53.698
If you want to bring a housewarming gift.
I love a good whiskey.

411
00:33:54.574 --> 00:33:55.575
[Kim] All right.

412
00:33:56.325 --> 00:33:57.910
I'll bring you the strongest I have.

413
00:34:00.371 --> 00:34:02.123
[chuckles] Can't wait.

414
00:34:03.583 --> 00:34:05.460
I'm already getting a bit thirsty.

415
00:34:06.044 --> 00:34:08.254
You better come at me
with everything you've got.

416
00:34:14.969 --> 00:34:17.722
I'm just saying.
isn't this taking it too far?

417
00:34:17.805 --> 00:34:19.557
Using a kid like this? Huh?

418
00:34:20.349 --> 00:34:21.559
This is wrong.

419
00:34:21.642 --> 00:34:23.853
[sighs] What the hell am I saying?

420
00:34:23.936 --> 00:34:26.397
[breathing deeply]

421
00:34:26.481 --> 00:34:27.774
I am an agent.

422
00:34:28.649 --> 00:34:30.401
I am an agent.

423
00:34:30.485 --> 00:34:32.653
I'm not a dry cleaner.
That's not who I am.

424
00:34:32.737 --> 00:34:35.114
No! What I amâ€¦ is an agent.

425
00:34:35.198 --> 00:34:38.367
I am an agent. I just work
as a dry cleaner. but I'm an agent!

426
00:34:38.451 --> 00:34:39.702
[groans]

427
00:34:39.786 --> 00:34:41.454
I need to get myself together.

428
00:34:44.582 --> 00:34:46.084
ONCE A MARINE. ALWAYS A MARINE

429
00:34:59.764 --> 00:35:00.765
[groans]

430
00:35:01.390 --> 00:35:02.391
Tae kwon do.

431
00:35:06.187 --> 00:35:07.188
[screams. distorted]

432
00:35:07.271 --> 00:35:09.398
I should've snapped both his scrawny legs.

433
00:35:13.319 --> 00:35:15.029
[gasps. screaming]

434
00:35:30.253 --> 00:35:31.462
[beast growls]

435
00:35:53.901 --> 00:35:54.944
Attention!

436
00:35:57.572 --> 00:35:59.365
Hey. pookie.

437
00:35:59.448 --> 00:36:01.200
Honey. what are you doing here?

438
00:36:01.284 --> 00:36:03.244
A-And what's with the knife. sweetheart?

439
00:36:03.327 --> 00:36:04.912
Well. you haven't come home in three days

440
00:36:04.996 --> 00:36:08.124
so I came to see if you started
a new family or something.

441
00:36:08.207 --> 00:36:09.208
Ah. geez.

442
00:36:10.835 --> 00:36:11.836
[grunts]

443
00:36:14.213 --> 00:36:16.257
But judging by the looks of things.

444
00:36:16.340 --> 00:36:18.676
it doesn't seem like
you're cheating or anything.

445
00:36:18.759 --> 00:36:22.221
What? Why would I cheat on you?
Do you think I'm crazy?

446
00:36:22.305 --> 00:36:23.931
I-I mean. you promised in our wedding vows

447
00:36:24.015 --> 00:36:25.892
that if I ever cheated on you.
you'd have me shot.

448
00:36:32.815 --> 00:36:34.525
I accept that answer.

449
00:36:34.609 --> 00:36:38.863
So then. what's your excuse
for staying out for so long. soldier?

450
00:36:38.946 --> 00:36:40.323
Yes. ma'am!

451
00:36:40.406 --> 00:36:42.366
You know I'm not the type of guy
to stay out all night.

452
00:36:42.450 --> 00:36:44.410
But Kim's daughter was kidnapped
out of nowhere.

453
00:36:44.493 --> 00:36:45.786
[distorted] You know Min-ji. right?

454
00:36:45.870 --> 00:36:47.246
Why was she kidnapped?
That's a long story.

455
00:36:47.330 --> 00:36:49.123
But anyways. I was in the holding cell.
so I got there late.

456
00:36:49.207 --> 00:36:50.958
And then there were some bad guys
who insulted our daughter.

457
00:36:51.042 --> 00:36:52.501
-What?
-[normal] That's what I'm saying!

458
00:36:52.585 --> 00:36:53.586
Why bring up Da-bin?

459
00:36:53.669 --> 00:36:55.338
[distorted] I should've taught them
a lesson then and there!

460
00:36:55.421 --> 00:36:57.215
But the police showed up
and tased me. [imitates Taser]

461
00:36:57.298 --> 00:36:58.799
Man. I forgot
how much Tasers actually hurt.

462
00:36:58.883 --> 00:37:00.343
And then Han-soo was there!

463
00:37:00.426 --> 00:37:01.928
He was trying to help
but fell into the water.

464
00:37:02.011 --> 00:37:04.722
[laughs] I didn't know
he was such a bad swimmer.

465
00:37:04.805 --> 00:37:06.265
Anyway. so I was on my wayâ€¦ Wait a sec

466
00:37:06.349 --> 00:37:08.851
But first I went to a rest area
and bought a germanium braceletâ€¦

467
00:37:08.935 --> 00:37:10.144
Didn't get me one?

468
00:37:10.228 --> 00:37:11.604
[normal] Oh. actually. this one's for you.

469
00:37:11.687 --> 00:37:12.897
[distorted]
I don't know if it works. though.

470
00:37:12.980 --> 00:37:14.982
So. anyway. I crossed mountains
and rivers just to make it here.

471
00:37:15.066 --> 00:37:16.734
Why did I come here? 'Causeâ€¦

472
00:37:16.817 --> 00:37:19.153
[normal] Oh. right!
The weapons! [chuckles]

473
00:37:19.237 --> 00:37:20.696
I'm here to get the weapons.

474
00:37:20.780 --> 00:37:22.031
Hold on.

475
00:37:23.115 --> 00:37:26.994
Kim's daughter was kidnapped. so you
and Sung Han-soo are going to go with Kim

476
00:37:27.078 --> 00:37:28.579
to try to rescue his daughter?

477
00:37:28.663 --> 00:37:33.334
Exactly! Man. you're so smart.
Oh. my wife is such a genius. [chuckles]

478
00:37:33.417 --> 00:37:36.921
So. yeah. I was thinking of goingâ€¦

479
00:37:37.004 --> 00:37:39.215
-but I really shouldn't.
-[beast growls]

480
00:37:39.298 --> 00:37:40.758
Forgive me. ma'am.

481
00:37:51.185 --> 00:37:53.938
-Who the hell beat you up like this?
-It was self-inflicted. ma'am.

482
00:37:56.857 --> 00:37:57.858
Help him.

483
00:38:01.237 --> 00:38:02.571
Likeâ€¦

484
00:38:02.655 --> 00:38:03.656
I can go?

485
00:38:05.032 --> 00:38:06.284
You guys went to war together

486
00:38:07.034 --> 00:38:08.619
No matter what I say. you're gonna go.

487
00:38:09.870 --> 00:38:12.665
Just bring me <i>tteokbokki </i>after.
Extra sauce.

488
00:38:15.209 --> 00:38:16.669
Spiciness level two. ma'am?

489
00:38:17.378 --> 00:38:18.379
Add some cheese too.

490
00:38:19.005 --> 00:38:20.006
Cheese! Got it!

491
00:38:20.089 --> 00:38:22.842
And will you please go change
out of your clothes? You smell.

492
00:38:22.925 --> 00:38:23.926
Ugh. What is that?

493
00:38:24.969 --> 00:38:26.012
Whatever. I don't care.

494
00:38:26.971 --> 00:38:28.514
Don't worry. I'll be safe. okay?

495
00:38:30.057 --> 00:38:31.767
Why would I worry about you?

496
00:38:31.851 --> 00:38:33.978
I'm more worried
about the idiots you're fighting.

497
00:38:34.687 --> 00:38:37.481
When will you guys realize
you're too old for this?

498
00:38:37.565 --> 00:38:39.608
[sighs]

499
00:38:41.986 --> 00:38:43.195
I love you. ma'am.

500
00:38:43.279 --> 00:38:44.280
Attention!

501
00:38:46.449 --> 00:38:47.533
[exhales heavily]

502
00:38:59.754 --> 00:39:01.130
Oh. my goodness.

503
00:39:02.631 --> 00:39:03.966
I almost died.

504
00:39:04.050 --> 00:39:05.634
That could've been it for me.

505
00:39:07.303 --> 00:39:08.596
Took ten years off my life.

506
00:39:09.805 --> 00:39:10.806
[grunts]

507
00:39:10.890 --> 00:39:11.891
